WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.620
SpaceX Dragon Experiments on artificial retinas and brain tissue now run and sustain microgravity aboard the station. This is SpaceX Daily Episode 133. Harmony Modules Space Facing Port received a SpaceX Dragon cargo craft at 10.27 am, Eastern Daylight Time on October 15th, Science Daily Reports on the International Space Station, or ISS. Cargo Mastop 6,300 pounds of supplies and research gear on commercial resupply flight 35.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:37.480
Also on board was the last pair of rollout solar arrays, headed for a later install that will raise station electrical capacity.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:43.920
Microgravity manufacturing of artificial retinas aims to improve structures for restoring vision on Earth,

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.220
while three-dimensional heart tissue models will support large-scale drug testing.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:55.560
Brain organoids, miniature lab-grown neural clusters, will be used to study targets for Alzheimer's, Parkinson's,

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.460
and multiple sclerosis treatments, and a new glass formation experiment will examine

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.840
how the material behaves with gravity removed.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:08.300
The spacecraft stays attached through mid-November, and this arrival continues a sequence of

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:13.480
dragon missions that have now delivered more than 35 resupply payloads under the National

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.640
Aeronautics and Space Administration, or NASA, contract.

00:01:17.717 --> 00:01:23.557
SpaceX will release 3rd quarter, 2020 financial and operational results on October 20.

00:01:23.557 --> 00:01:26.117
It's first earnings as a public company.

00:01:26.577 --> 00:01:32.277
A live audio-only webcast is scheduled for 3.30pm central time that same day, according

00:01:32.277 --> 00:01:34.497
to the company's investor relations page.

00:01:35.017 --> 00:01:39.537
The release will cover financial metrics and operational updates across launch, star

00:01:39.537 --> 00:01:41.057
link, and dragon programs.

00:01:41.857 --> 00:01:45.777
Investors and analysts have tracked the cadence of these quarterly updates since the company

00:01:45.777 --> 00:01:47.837
listed on NASDAQ earlier this year.

00:01:47.837 --> 00:01:54.204
Super Heavy Booster 23 finished a cryogenic proof test at Massie's site on October 15,

00:01:54.844 --> 00:01:58.224
according to a post on X that has not been independently confirmed.

00:01:58.664 --> 00:02:00.884
The run is a cold propellant pressure check.

00:02:01.324 --> 00:02:05.164
It asks whether the tanks hold under the thermal and pressure loads of flight.

00:02:05.824 --> 00:02:10.744
Booster 23 now joins a growing fleet of vehicles moving through the star-based production and

00:02:10.744 --> 00:02:11.324
test flow.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:17.660
Cursor shipped its environment's API or application programming interface in beta so

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:22.520
So developers can create and manage cloud agent environments by code, including repo

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.700
cloning and environment JSON setup.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:30.480
Cloud agent environments now support up to 500 repos and start large multi repo setups

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.760
five times faster.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.880
The company said in a post on X.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.920
The change extends how far the platform can orchestrate agent workspaces at scale.

00:02:39.954 --> 00:02:44.294
Elon Musk said the next Roadster will perform autonomous tricks and run a looping track

00:02:44.294 --> 00:02:45.494
at Texas headquarters.

00:02:46.114 --> 00:02:53.954
Owners will be able to request any trick already demonstrated, and the car will run it on its own, he wrote on X, calling the vehicle sentient.

00:02:54.514 --> 00:03:00.934
He described that looping track as more extreme than hot wheels and tied the car to autonomous control systems under development.

00:03:02.025 --> 00:03:08.265
Optimus will build Optimus Prime, Elon Musk posted in a short note on X on October 17th.

00:03:08.265 --> 00:03:12.225
The remark points to future manufacturing roles for the humanoid robot line.

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:17.505
Blue Origin will add new Florida launch pads and two landing ships to raise new Glenn's

00:03:17.505 --> 00:03:19.805
flight rate, space flight now reports.

00:03:20.265 --> 00:03:24.745
Those pads are meant to support multiple flights per week by the end of the decade, and

00:03:24.745 --> 00:03:30.965
a 1.37 million square foot factory will produce up to 150 upper stages a year once it is

00:03:30.965 --> 00:03:33.045
complete in summer 2027.

00:03:33.685 --> 00:03:39.465
The company is putting $330 million into the Rocket Park expansion and plans a new vertical

00:03:39.465 --> 00:03:44.925
integration building plus a payload processing facility. Blue Origin has already placed more

00:03:44.925 --> 00:03:50.385
than $3 billion in Florida infrastructure and employs more than 5,000 people in the state

00:03:50.385 --> 00:03:55.865
with support from 500 suppliers. The Federal Aviation Administration, or FAA,

00:03:56.145 --> 00:04:02.125
is reviewing a request to raise permitted flights at Launch Complex 36A from 12 to 50

00:04:02.125 --> 00:04:08.693
during a 30-day public comment period. Space Launch System, or SLS, production is expected to

00:04:08.693 --> 00:04:13.693
continue for only two to three more years. Launch analyst Saigai Space said on October

00:04:13.693 --> 00:04:19.673
16th, offering a personal assessment rather than an official NASA timeline. That view reflects

00:04:19.673 --> 00:04:24.773
current congressional and NASA planning for the heavy-lift vehicle. Worth keeping an eye on,

00:04:24.993 --> 00:04:29.673
Vodafone has taken formal concerns about SpaceX's spectrum use to regulators and Brussels,

00:04:30.233 --> 00:04:35.593
while several Wall Street firms maintain positive ratings on the company. The filing underscores

00:04:35.593 --> 00:04:41.493
ongoing European pushback on starlink licensing and interference claims, ad hoc news reports.

00:04:42.113 --> 00:04:46.673
Resolution would require coordination between national regulators and the European Commission.

00:04:47.333 --> 00:04:51.673
European operators continue to press for technical studies on signal overlap before

00:04:51.673 --> 00:04:57.371
additional approvals advance. For the tissue payloads now on station, the engineering reality

00:04:57.371 --> 00:05:03.991
is that gravity itself is a process contaminant. On Earth, everything in a flask feels 9.8 meters per

00:05:03.991 --> 00:05:09.671
second squared, and denser clumps sediment while warmer, lighter fluid rises. Those two

00:05:09.671 --> 00:05:15.231
motions, sedimentation and buoyancy convection, never stop, and they smear the layers biologists

00:05:15.231 --> 00:05:21.171
are trying to build. Take a cell about 10 micrometers across, with a mass on the order of 1 nanogram.

00:05:21.851 --> 00:05:26.911
A back of envelope stokes estimate puts its settling speed on the ground on the order of 1 micrometer

00:05:26.911 --> 00:05:33.371
per second, so a 1mm stack can crush or scramble in roughly 15 minutes. On station,

00:05:33.371 --> 00:05:38.931
Residual acceleration is on the order of 1 millionth of G, so that same settling time stretches

00:05:38.931 --> 00:05:44.591
by a factor of about a million, weeks instead of minutes, which is why photoreceptor precursors

00:05:44.591 --> 00:05:47.371
can sit in radial layers instead of a packed sludge.

00:05:47.871 --> 00:05:49.691
Nutrient transport flips with it.

00:05:50.031 --> 00:05:54.911
Protein-sized molecules diffuse through water at roughly 10 to the power of minus 6 square

00:05:54.911 --> 00:06:00.111
centimeters per second, so crossing a millimeter of still media takes on the order of 3 hours.

00:06:00.111 --> 00:06:05.911
On the ground, buoyancy-driven eddies mix that volume in seconds, but the mixing is patchy.

00:06:06.331 --> 00:06:11.391
In orbit, the convective term is gone, so the only even supply is a pump, which is why

00:06:11.391 --> 00:06:16.631
these runs need perfusion loops, forced media flow, size to replace the missing convection

00:06:16.631 --> 00:06:17.671
rather than fight it.

00:06:18.231 --> 00:06:22.251
Heart muscle cells, cardiomyocytes, gain for a different mechanical reason.

00:06:22.811 --> 00:06:27.771
In one G, they sit under their own compressive load, which changes how gap junctions form

00:06:27.771 --> 00:06:29.611
and how electrical coupling spreads.

00:06:30.191 --> 00:06:31.711
Unload that stress and alignment

00:06:31.711 --> 00:06:33.511
can run across larger volumes.

00:06:34.031 --> 00:06:35.691
Glass melts see the same physics

00:06:35.691 --> 00:06:36.911
from the material side.

00:06:37.491 --> 00:06:39.431
Density-driven currents that normally sweep

00:06:39.431 --> 00:06:41.231
early crystals around are absent,

00:06:41.651 --> 00:06:43.411
so nucleation rates can be measured

00:06:43.411 --> 00:06:45.631
as a function of chemistry rather than stirring.

00:06:46.351 --> 00:06:48.811
Thermal control has to hold incubator set points

00:06:48.811 --> 00:06:51.491
near 37 degrees Celsius inside dragon

00:06:51.491 --> 00:06:53.511
and the station's express racks

00:06:53.511 --> 00:06:55.311
because a few degrees of drift

00:06:55.311 --> 00:06:59.691
kills viability over weeks. Power for those racks and pumps is the other

00:06:59.691 --> 00:07:03.991
constraint. An extra margin from the arriving arrays is what keeps sensitive

00:07:03.991 --> 00:07:08.251
payloads from competing with station house keeping. The magic wand inputs

00:07:08.251 --> 00:07:13.331
ourselves, sterile media, and a few tens of watts. The idiot index on the ground

00:07:13.331 --> 00:07:17.971
is ugly. If settling ruins even half the retinal stacks, you have paid twice

00:07:17.971 --> 00:07:22.311
the media and labor per good part. Data from this flight is meant to put a

00:07:22.311 --> 00:07:24.731
number on how much of that waste was just gravity.

